# Fix Dashboard Layout Shift After Onboarding Timer Starts

## Problem
After onboarding starts the timer and the Kanban board appears, there's ~300px of white space on the left side of the viewport. The content is shifted to the right.

## Root Cause
In `dashboard.css`, `.dashboard-container` has `justify-content: center`:

```css
.dashboard-container {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;  /* <-- PROBLEM */
  position: relative;
}
```

This centering is needed during onboarding to center the ticket card. But when `showKanban` becomes true and the Kanban wrapper is rendered, the centering still applies, pushing the full-width Kanban content to the center instead of the left edge.

## Files to Modify
1. `frontend/src/app/dashboard/page.tsx` - Add conditional class
2. `frontend/src/app/dashboard/dashboard.css` - Move centering to conditional class

## Fix

### 1. Update CSS (`dashboard.css`)
Remove `justify-content: center` from `.dashboard-container` and add it to a modifier class:

```css
.dashboard-container {
  min-height: 100vh;
  background-color: transparent;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  /* Remove: justify-content: center; */
  position: relative;
}

.dashboard-container--centered {
  justify-content: center;
}
```

### 2. Update TSX (`page.tsx`)
Apply the `--centered` modifier only when showing onboarding without the kanban:

```tsx
// Line 54: When showing onboarding
<div className={`dashboard-container${!showKanban ? ' dashboard-container--centered' : ''}`}>

// Line 71: When not showing onboarding (regular dashboard)
<div className="dashboard-container">
```

## Logic
- During onboarding (before timer starts): `showKanban=false` → apply `--centered` → ticket card is centered ✓
- After timer starts and kanban appears: `showKanban=true` → no `--centered` → kanban fills from left edge ✓
- Regular dashboard (onboarding complete): no `--centered` → kanban fills from left edge ✓
